<div class="collection-page">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="collection-page__header">
      <h1 class="collection-page__title">{{ collection.title }}</h1>
      {%- if collection.description != blank -%}
        <p class="collection-page__desc">{{ collection.description }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Lives inside the Filter panel only now (the "Shop by category" group
      below) — a standalone row above the toolbar duplicated it for no
      reason once the panel had its own copy. Still captured here rather
      than rendered inline in the panel markup, so the "does the Filter
      button need to render at all" check further down can test it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture category_pills -%}{%- render 'category-pills', current: collection -%}{%- endcapture -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Filters and sort share one GET form and one submit, so applying a
      filter doesn't reset the sort order (or vice versa) the way two
      separate forms fighting over the same query string would.

      collection.filters comes from whatever's configured as a storefront
      filter in Admin → Search & Discovery — it's empty until that's set up,
      in which case the Filter button doesn't render at all and this is
      just the sort-only toolbar. Nothing here needs an app or a hardcoded
      list of tags to keep working as that configuration changes.

      The filter panel is one <details> (a single "Filter" button, like a
      normal storefront) rather than one per filter group — group headings
      inside stay as plain <h3>s, not their own toggles, so opening the
      panel shows everything at once instead of a row of separate
      accordions. Checkboxes and the price range don't auto-submit here:
      inside a multi-select panel, submitting on every click would reload
      the page — and close the panel — before a second box could be
      checked. Sort is still its own auto-submitting control outside the
      panel, where an immediate reload is exactly what a single dropdown
      should do.

      A filter value that every product in the current collection already
      carries (count == collection.products_count) narrows nothing if
      checked — same result either way. Rather than curate that per school
      in Search & Discovery (which only gets more tags to babysit as more
      schools are added), values like that are skipped here unless already
      active, so unchecking one that's somehow on still works. This is
      driven entirely by live counts, so it needs no maintenance as new
      schools/sports/opponents are added.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign sort_current = collection.sort_by | default: collection.default_sort_by -%}
    {%- assign active_filter_count = 0 -%}
    {%- for filter in collection.filters -%}
      {%- assign active_filter_count = active_filter_count | plus: filter.active_values.size -%}
      {%- if filter.min_value.value != nil or filter.max_value.value != nil -%}
        {%- assign active_filter_count = active_filter_count | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      The Filter button shows whenever there's something to put in it —
      real storefront filters, category links, or both — rather than only
      when collection.filters happens to be configured. Otherwise the
      category group would silently disappear if Search & Discovery
      filters were ever turned off.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign show_filter_button = false -%}
    {%- if section.settings.show_filters and collection.filters.size > 0 -%}
      {%- assign show_filter_button = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if category_pills != blank -%}
      {%- assign show_filter_button = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    <form method="get" action="{{ collection.url }}" class="collection-toolbar">
      <div class="collection-toolbar__row">
        <p class="collection-toolbar__count">
          {{ collection.products_count }}
          {%- if collection.products_count == 1 -%} product{%- else -%} products{%- endif -%}
        </p>

        <div class="collection-toolbar__controls">
          {%- if show_filter_button -%}
            <details class="filter-panel" data-filter-panel>
              <summary class="filter-panel__toggle">
                <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="4" y1="6" x2="20" y2="6"/><line x1="7" y1="12" x2="17" y2="12"/><line x1="10" y1="18" x2="14" y2="18"/></svg>
                Filter
                {%- if active_filter_count > 0 %} <span class="filter-panel__count">{{ active_filter_count }}</span>{% endif -%}
              </summary>

              <div class="filter-panel__body">
                {%- if category_pills != blank -%}
                  <div class="filter-panel__group">
                    <p class="label filter-panel__group-title">Shop by category</p>
                    <div class="category-pills category-pills--compact">{{ category_pills }}</div>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- for filter in collection.filters -%}
                  {%- comment -%}
                    The hyphen rule below only applies to the tags filter
                    (param_name "filter.v.tag") — Availability, Price, and
                    any future Size/Color/Vendor filter keep the plain
                    count-based show/hide rule untouched, since a bare
                    "true" or "Small" isn't standing in for a pill and
                    shouldn't be judged as if it were.

                    Within the tags filter specifically: a plain,
                    unhyphenated tag (auburn, football, sorority) is what
                    the category pills' hierarchy is already built from —
                    showing it again as a checkbox just duplicates the
                    pill that does the same job better (a real page,
                    shareable, with its own further filtering), so plain
                    tags never render here. Only a "facet-value" tag
                    (opponent-vanderbilt, chapter-kappa-delta, ...) is a
                    genuine cross-cutting refinement that pills can't
                    express, so those are the only checkboxes this filter
                    ever shows — plus anything already active, so a filter
                    somehow applied via URL is still visible and clearable
                    rather than silently stuck on.

                    Group label: defaults to whatever's set in Search &
                    Discovery, but when every value shown here shares the
                    same facet prefix, that facet becomes the label
                    instead — titlecased, read straight off the tag. A new
                    facet gets a correct label the moment products are
                    tagged that way; nothing here needs to know the word
                    "opponent" or "chapter" ahead of time.
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  {%- assign is_tag_filter = false -%}
                  {%- if filter.param_name == 'filter.v.tag' -%}
                    {%- assign is_tag_filter = true -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- assign group_label = filter.label -%}
                  {%- assign shared_facet = '' -%}
                  {%- assign facet_mismatch = false -%}
                  {%- assign visible_value_count = 0 -%}
                  {%- for filter_value in filter.values -%}
                    {%- assign show_this_value = false -%}
                    {%- if filter_value.active -%}
                      {%- assign show_this_value = true -%}
                    {%- elsif is_tag_filter and filter_value.value contains '-' and filter_value.count > 0 and filter_value.count < collection.products_count -%}
                      {%- assign show_this_value = true -%}
                    {%- elsif is_tag_filter == false and filter_value.count > 0 and filter_value.count < collection.products_count -%}
                      {%- assign show_this_value = true -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {%- if show_this_value -%}
                      {%- assign visible_value_count = visible_value_count | plus: 1 -%}
                      {%- assign value_parts = filter_value.value | split: '-' -%}
                      {%- assign this_facet = '' -%}
                      {%- if value_parts.size > 1 -%}
                        {%- assign this_facet = value_parts | first -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {%- if this_facet == blank -%}
                        {%- assign facet_mismatch = true -%}
                      {%- elsif shared_facet == blank -%}
                        {%- assign shared_facet = this_facet -%}
                      {%- elsif shared_facet != this_facet -%}
                        {%- assign facet_mismatch = true -%}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- if visible_value_count > 0 and facet_mismatch == false and shared_facet != blank -%}
                    {%- assign group_label = shared_facet | capitalize -%}
                  {%- endif -%}

                  <div class="filter-panel__group">
                    <p class="label filter-panel__group-title">{{ group_label }}</p>
                    {%- comment -%} TEMP DEBUG — remove after diagnosing {%- endcomment -%}
                    <!-- FILTER-DEBUG param={{ filter.param_name }} type={{ filter.type }} is_tag_filter={{ is_tag_filter }}{% for fv in filter.values %} || value=[{{ fv.value }}] label=[{{ fv.label }}] count={{ fv.count }} active={{ fv.active }}{% endfor %} -->

                    {%- case filter.type -%}
                      {%- when 'list' or 'boolean' -%}
                        <ul class="filter-panel__options" role="list">
                          {%- for filter_value in filter.values -%}
                            {%- assign show_filter_value = false -%}
                            {%- if filter_value.active -%}
                              {%- assign show_filter_value = true -%}
                            {%- elsif is_tag_filter and filter_value.value contains '-' and filter_value.count > 0 and filter_value.count < collection.products_count -%}
                              {%- assign show_filter_value = true -%}
                            {%- elsif is_tag_filter == false and filter_value.count > 0 and filter_value.count < collection.products_count -%}
                              {%- assign show_filter_value = true -%}
                            {%- endif -%}
                            {%- if show_filter_value -%}
                              <li class="filter-panel__option">
                                <label>
                                  <input
                                    type="checkbox"
                                    name="{{ filter_value.param_name }}"
                                    value="{{ filter_value.value }}"
                                    {% if filter_value.active %}checked{% endif %}
                                  >
                                  <span>{{ filter_value.label }} <span class="filter-panel__option-count">({{ filter_value.count }})</span></span>
                                </label>
                              </li>
                            {%- endif -%}
                          {%- endfor -%}
                        </ul>
                      {%- when 'price_range' -%}
                        <div class="filter-panel__price">
                          <label class="filter-panel__price-field">
                            <span class="visually-hidden">Minimum price</span>
                            <span aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.currency.symbol }}</span>
                            <input
                              type="number"
                              name="{{ filter.min_value.param_name }}"
                              value="{{ filter.min_value.value }}"
                              placeholder="{{ filter.range_min | money_without_currency }}"
                              min="0"
                            >
                          </label>
                          <span class="filter-panel__price-sep" aria-hidden="true">–</span>
                          <label class="filter-panel__price-field">
                            <span class="visually-hidden">Maximum price</span>
                            <span aria-hidden="true">{{ cart.currency.symbol }}</span>
                            <input
                              type="number"
                              name="{{ filter.max_value.param_name }}"
                              value="{{ filter.max_value.value }}"
                              placeholder="{{ filter.range_max | money_without_currency }}"
                              min="0"
                            >
                          </label>
                        </div>
                    {%- endcase -%}
                  </div>
                {%- endfor -%}

                {%- if section.settings.show_filters and collection.filters.size > 0 -%}
                  <div class="filter-panel__actions">
                    <button type="submit" class="btn btn--primary btn--sm">Apply</button>
                    {%- if active_filter_count > 0 -%}
                      <a href="{{ collection.url }}{% if sort_current != collection.default_sort_by %}?sort_by={{ sort_current }}{% endif %}" class="filter-panel__clear">
                        Clear all
                      </a>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </details>
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if section.settings.show_sort and collection.sort_options.size > 0 -%}
            <div class="collection-toolbar__sort" data-auto-submit>
              <label for="sort-by">Sort by</label>
              <select name="sort_by" id="sort-by">
                {%- for option in collection.sort_options -%}
                  <option value="{{ option.value }}"{% if option.value == sort_current %} selected{% endif %}>{{ option.name }}</option>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </select>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      <noscript><button type="submit" class="btn btn--outline btn--sm">Apply</button></noscript>
    </form>

    {%- paginate collection.products by section.settings.products_per_page -%}
      {%- if collection.products.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="product-grid">
          {%- for product in collection.products -%}
            {%- render 'product-card', product: product -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>

        {%- if paginate.pages > 1 -%}
          <nav class="pagination" aria-label="Pagination">
            {%- if paginate.previous -%}
              <a href="{{ paginate.previous.url }}" class="btn btn--outline btn--sm" rel="prev">← Previous</a>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- for part in paginate.parts -%}
              {%- if part.is_link -%}
                <a href="{{ part.url }}" class="btn btn--outline btn--sm" aria-label="Page {{ part.title }}">{{ part.title }}</a>
              {%- elsif part.title == paginate.current_page -%}
                <span class="btn btn--primary btn--sm" aria-current="page">{{ part.title }}</span>
              {%- else -%}
                <span class="btn btn--outline btn--sm pagination__gap" aria-hidden="true">{{ part.title }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
            {%- if paginate.next -%}
              <a href="{{ paginate.next.url }}" class="btn btn--outline btn--sm" rel="next">Next →</a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </nav>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- else -%}
        <p class="collection-page__empty">No products found in this collection.</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endpaginate -%}
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collection Grid",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "products_per_page",
      "label": "Products per Page",
      "min": 8,
      "max": 48,
      "step": 4,
      "default": 24
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_sort",
      "label": "Show Sort Dropdown",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "show_filters",
      "label": "Show Filters",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Filters are configured in Search & Discovery under Admin → Online Store. Nothing shows here until at least one is set up there."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
